			"SHA": "7929e37e80952d8935362f0b51d182161aa99631"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T23:36:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				739,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Resolve WKWebView font blocking and API injection failures\n\nExtend the `Logging` transform plugin to address two critical webview rendering issues on WKWebView (Tauri):\n\n1. **CSP Font Fallback**: Inject a `font-src *` wildcard fallback into the Content Security Policy rewrite logic. WKWebView silently blocks fonts (e.g., KaTeX, Codicons) when custom protocol schemes like `vscode-file:` are used in `font-src` without a wildcard match.\n\n2. **Mandatory API Injection**: Force the injection of the `_vscodeApiScript` (providing `acquireVsCodeApi`) regardless of the `options.allowScripts` flag. Diagnostics revealed that when `allowScripts` is false, the API script was skipped, causing extensions like Roo Code to fail initialization despite module scripts executing.\n\nAdditionally, correct a missing closing brace in `RuntimeDiagnosticsInner.js` and update `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to include external links and enhanced formatting for the Output package documentation.\n\nThese changes restore full functionality for font rendering and extension host APIs in cross-platform webview environments.",
			"SHA": "ee4c445d3826501c3fcaeb48e6b9d01fb22f5744"
		}
	],
